WEB SOURCE (the specification — read end to end)
  web/src/features/trips/components/TripReplayMap.tsx — "a thin wrapper around the trip-replay leaflet map" that
  composes LOW-LEVEL @/components/maps primitives (MapContainer / Polyline / CircleMarker / AnimatedMarker /
  MapTileLayer / MapLayerSwitcher / FitBounds / useMap). It is a presentational leaf fed by its parent drive-detail
  page via props (positions[], currentIndex, onSeekToIndex, reduceMotion, initialMapStyle, height); the page stays the
  single source of truth so scrubber / chart cursor / map marker stay in lockstep.

    Render branches:
      positions.length > 0 → <MapContainer> with:
        • FitBounds(trail, fallbackCenter=anchorPoint)  — fit bbox; collapse → setView(anchor,15); else fallback.
        • speed-coloured Polyline segments (only when hasMeaningfulRoute) — one polyline per consecutive pair,
          colour = speedColor(curr.speed ?? 0); each polyline's click → handlePolylineClick.
        • start CircleMarker (#10b981) + end CircleMarker (#ef4444) when hasRoute.
        • single anchor CircleMarker (#22d3ee) when NOT hasRoute (stationary GPS).
        • playhead: AnimatedMarker(position=currentPosition, heading) when !reduceMotion, else a plain
          CircleMarker (#00b4d8) — tracks currentIndex exclusively (no internal playback state).
        • MapLayerSwitcher (bottom) + the stationary-GPS AlertBanner overlaid at top when !hasRoute.
      positions.length === 0 → <EmptyState icon=MapPin message=t('replay.map.noPositions', …)>.

  Hooks / helpers (the contract — reproduced verbatim, arithmetic NOT "fixed"):
    useMap (leaflet ctx, drives FitBounds) · useTranslation.
    geo.ts: haversineDistance (R=6_371_000 m) · MIN_MEANINGFUL_ROUTE_METERS=10 · isValidLatLng (finite, not (0,0),
            lat∈[-90,90], lng∈[-180,180]) · hasMeaningfulRoute (anchor scan, ≥10 m) · firstValidIndex (-1 if none).
    component: speedColor(kmh) = <30 green · <60 cyan · <100 amber · else red ;
               computeHeading(p1,p2) = initial great-circle bearing, normalised [0,360) ;
               nearestSampleIndex(positions, lat, lng) = O(n) min-haversine, empty ⇒ 0 ;
               heading: next = i<n-1 ? i+1 : i ; prev = next>0 ? next-1 : 0 ; computeHeading(prev,next) ;
               currentPosition = hasRoute ? positions[currentIndex] ?? null : null ;
               centerPos = startPos ?? anchorPoint ?? [47.6, -122.3].
  i18n (the three t() keys extracted from source):
    replay.map.stationaryRouteTitle = "Route can't be plotted"
    replay.map.stationaryRouteBody  = "Only one GPS coordinate was recorded for this drive, so the route can't be
                                       drawn. The trip statistics, speed, and elevation timeline above the scrubber
                                       are unaffected."
    replay.map.noPositions          = "No position data available for this drive"

